    {
      "id": "p00018",
      "text": "He vainly said that human will is free, and that he chose neither\nthe one nor the other. He was forced to make a choice; he determined, in\nvirtue of that gift of God called liberty, to run the gauntlet\nsix-and-thirty times. He bore this twice.",
      "translation": "Il eut beau\ndire que les volontés sont libres, et qu’il ne voulait ni l’un ni\nl’autre, il fallut faire un choix; il se détermina, en vertu du don de\nDieu qu’on nomme _liberté_, à passer trente-six fois par les baguettes;\nil essuya deux promenades.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p00018",
      "target_paragraph_id": "fr-p00002",
      "languages": {
        "base": "en",
        "learning": "fr"
      },
      "replacements": [],
      "sentences": []
    },
